Map chemical origins without confusing a substance with one production route (@cs-origins: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @chemical-supply-systems, #source "../../../chemistry/industrial-chemistry/sources/Inorganic-Chemical-Technology-Kishore.lingua#r_77Z8T5RFYFNNXZ7XKZFKPRKDKR", #source "../../../chemistry/industrial-chemistry/sources/Organic-Chemical-Technology-Kishore.lingua#r_1ERYESBGNKCKMDY0NPHJKCVJG0", #source "../sources/Chemical-Supply-Chain-Profiles-EPA.lingua#r_0E09Q6T7CC9HNWZB3N84E7K21A", #chemical-supply-systems "Mineral-and-brine-feeds-to-industrial-chemical-users.lingua#r_3WHQXNXP7EJ36X35N599P0D3XB") { r_18DV5AVKV5YFZEB77Z5SHBYYCT
**Read:** [Inorganic Chemical Technology — Nanda Kishore, NPTEL](../../../chemistry/industrial-chemistry/sources/Inorganic-Chemical-Technology-Kishore.lingua#r_77Z8T5RFYFNNXZ7XKZFKPRKDKR), the complete manufacturing progression, revisiting the named feed origins; [Organic Chemical Technology — Nanda Kishore, NPTEL](../../../chemistry/industrial-chemistry/sources/Organic-Chemical-Technology-Kishore.lingua#r_1ERYESBGNKCKMDY0NPHJKCVJG0), the complete course, including natural and synthetic feed families; [Water-treatment chemical supply-chain profiles — EPA](../sources/Chemical-Supply-Chain-Profiles-EPA.lingua#r_0E09Q6T7CC9HNWZB3N84E7K21A), complete profiles for contrasting mineral, carbon and air-derived inputs.

Build an origin map for ten materials used by different industries. Include mineral/brine sources, separated air products, water-derived inputs, fossil carbon, renewable carbon and recovered streams. For each material, state a useful chemical function, one actual manufacturing route, principal feed and co-products, and the evidence supporting the route. Use the existing industrial-chemistry sources rather than restating every process here.

Distinguish a stoichiometrically possible route from an established industrial supply, and a marketed product from installed capacity at the required grade and place. A renewable or recovered origin does not settle impurity, physical state, availability, environmental burden or compatibility with a user's process. A feedstock designation is always relative to a transformation.

Trace three levels upstream for two products. For example, an organic intermediate depends on chemical feeds and separations but also contact equipment, utilities, catalysts and analytical work. A mineral-derived acid can connect to mining, thermal processing and a by-product market. Mark uncertainty and multiple possible routes. Later family cases deepen selected paths; the map keeps the larger body of chemistry connected without requiring one reader to finish every neighbouring specialist subject first.

**Continue:** [Follow mineral and brine inputs through useful chemical grades](Mineral-and-brine-feeds-to-industrial-chemical-users.lingua#r_3WHQXNXP7EJ36X35N599P0D3XB).

